            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths in full. The change tightens the validator: --repo must be absolute (exit 2 otherwise) and must hold a .git entry (exit 7 otherwise). Both checks only add refusals and never turn a failure into a pass, so they cannot create a bypass or data exposure.",
              "checkRepositoryRoot uses os.Stat on caller-supplied paths only to test existence. It reads no content and writes nothing, and the validator is a local CLI tool, so there is no injection or traversal exposure.",
              "A .git file in a linked worktree is accepted by existence alone, and the change documents that git, not the validator, judges whether the repository is sound. A forged .git entry could only make the validator count results under a directory the caller already chose, so this opens no privilege boundary.",
              "The new tests (tools/actuals-record-validator/main_test.go) use t.TempDir and fixture strings only. No secrets or dependency changes are introduced, and no new modules are added.",
              "The CHANGELOG and README edits are documentation that matches the code behavior. No finding is raised."
            ]
          }
        }
