            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "tools/actuals-record-validator/main.go: the new filepath.IsAbs check runs after the required-flag check and before any file is read, so a relative --repo exits 2 with nothing validated. TestRelativeRepoExitsTwoAndChecksNothing covers both '.' and a relative path to a real repository root, and asserts the exit code, the message, and the absence of 'ok:'.",
              "tools/actuals-record-validator/main.go: checkRepositoryRoot returns an error for a missing path, a non-directory, or a directory without a .git entry. The caller maps all three to exit 7 with the path in the message. os.Stat follows links and accepts a .git file, so linked worktrees and submodules still pass. TestRepoThatIsNotTheRootOfARepositoryExitsSeven covers a plain directory and a subdirectory of a real repository, and TestRepoThatIsALinkedWorktreeRootIsAccepted covers the worktree case. All three assert exit code and path output.",
              "tools/actuals-record-validator/main_test.go: existing tests now use the newRepo helper, which creates a .git directory, so they keep exercising their original paths (exit 3, 4, 2, and the lens-count cases) rather than hitting the new exit 7.",
              "The documentation edits in odd/review-results/README.md and CHANGELOG.md match the new behavior: relative --repo gives exit 2, a missing .git gives exit 7, and the usage text agrees. The one behavior change worth noting is that a relative --repo combined with a bad schema or instance now exits 2 instead of 3 or 4. That is a usage-first ordering and is documented as a breaking change for callers."
            ]
          }
